#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:17
msgid "Face Winding Requirement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:19
msgid ""
"All algorithms below require that polyhedron faces have **outward-pointing "
"normals**: vertices must be ordered counter-clockwise when viewed from "
"outside the cell (right-hand rule). This requirement is documented in "
"`vtkPolyhedron.h`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:23
msgid ""
"The solid-angle `IsInside()` depends on this for correct sign of the winding "
"number. The López contour/clip algorithm depends on this for correct \"key "
"face\" assignment (outside→inside edge transitions)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:27
msgid "IsInside: Solid Angle Summation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:29
msgid ""
"`vtkPolyhedron::IsInside()` determines whether a query point lies inside or "
"outside the polyhedron using the winding number computed via solid angle "
"summation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:33
#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:77
#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:553
msgid "Algorithm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:35
msgid ""
"A closed surface subtends exactly **4π steradians** when viewed from any "
"interior point, and **0 steradians** from any exterior point. This is the 3D "
"generalization of the 2D winding number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:39
msgid ""
"total_solid_angle = 0\n"
"for each face:\n"
"    triangulate face (fan from minimum-index vertex)\n"
"    for each triangle (a, b, c):\n"
"        total_solid_angle += solid_angle(a, b, c, query_point)\n"
"\n"
"if |total_solid_angle| ≈ 4π → INSIDE\n"
"if |total_solid_angle| ≈ 0  → OUTSIDE\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:50
msgid ""
"The solid angle of a triangle is computed using the Van Oosterom–Strackee "
"formula:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:53
msgid ""
"tan(Ω/2) = det(ra, rb, rc) / (|ra||rb||rc| + |ra|(rb·rc) + |rb|(ra·rc) + |rc|"
"(ra·rb))\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:57
msgid "where `ra = a − x`, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:59
msgid ""
"A near-surface tolerance provides an early-out for points very close to "
"faces, treating them as inside. This avoids numerical ambiguity at the "
"boundary."
msgstr ""

