#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:163
msgid ""
"The old contour/clip bottleneck was `OrderEdgePolygon`, which performs a "
"linear scan plus `std::vector::erase` (both O(n)) for each edge in a face's "
"contour fragment, giving O(k²) per face. The new López algorithm visits each "
"iso-vertex exactly once during polygon tracing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:168
msgid ""
"The constant-factor improvement is also significant: the old implementation "
"creates ~20 intermediate data structures (vectors of edge vectors, edge-face "
"maps, point-edge multimaps, edge count maps) and converts between "
"representations multiple times. The new implementation uses one hash map for "
"edge-to-iso-vertex lookup and traces directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:173
msgid "Bulk Threaded API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:175
msgid ""
"`vtkPolyhedronContour` provides a per-cell static API for integration with "
"VTK's threaded contour and clip filters. The API takes the cell's "
"`vtkCellArray` face stream and a `vtkDataArray` scalar field directly, "
"without instantiating `vtkPolyhedron` objects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:180
msgid "Contour: single-call per-cell helper"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:182
msgid ""
"Contour extraction uses a single-pass cell helper, `ContourCell`. The helper "
"runs the full López trace for one polyhedron and reports the intersected "
"edges as `(globalPtId0, globalPtId1, t)` tuples plus a per-polygon vertex-"
"count array. Iso-vertex deduplication is performed by the calling filter "
"through its shared edge locator (`vtkStaticEdgeLocatorTemplate`); the helper "
"does not write final iso-vertex coordinates. There is no separate count "
"phase because `vtkContour3DLinearGrid` does not prefix-sum polyhedron cell "
"sizes before running the trace: the point merger absorbs per-cell output "
"into thread-local buffers, and the fast path emits triangle vertex "
"coordinates directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:193
msgid "Clip: two-pass Count/Emit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:195
msgid ""
"Clip uses the classic two-pass pattern required to deduplicate iso-vertices "
"through a shared edge locator:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:198
msgid ""
"**Count pass** (parallel): Each thread calls `CountClip` per cell to "
"determine output sizes and to record the set of intersected edges."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:201
msgid ""
"**Prefix sum + edge locator build** (serial): Global offsets are computed "
"from per-cell counts, and the collected edge list is fed into a shared "
"`vtkStaticEdgeLocatorTemplate` that assigns unique iso-vertex IDs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:205
msgid ""
"**Emit pass** (parallel): Each thread calls `EmitClip` per cell, writing "
"geometry into pre-allocated output arrays at the computed offsets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:208
msgid ""
"Both Count and Emit internally call the same `RunLopezTrace` function. The "
"trace is O(E). Running it twice per cell (once for Count, once for Emit) is "
"the canonical price paid for the two-pass parallel structure, and the thread-"
"local trace workspace keeps the constant factor low."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:213
msgid "Shared Core"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:215
msgid ""
"A single `RunLopezTrace` function in an anonymous namespace implements the "
"López algorithm on raw arrays. The per-cell `Execute` path and the bulk "
"entry points (`ContourCell`, `CountClip`, `EmitClip`) all dispatch through "
"this function. There is one algorithm implementation, not two."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:220
msgid "API Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:222
msgid ""
"All entry points take the cell's `vtkCellArray` face stream and a "
"`vtkDataArray` scalar directly, and report intersected edges as "
"`(globalPtId0, globalPtId1, t)` tuples for downstream deduplication via a "
"shared edge locator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:227
msgid ""
"**Contour — single-call helper.** Used by `vtkContour3DLinearGrid` in both "
"fast and general paths."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:230
msgid ""
"static void ContourCell(numPointIds, pointIds, polyhedronFaces, scalars,\n"
"    isoValue, generateTriangles,\n"
"    polygonsSize, intersectedEdges);\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:236
msgid ""
"`polygonsSize` is a per-output-polygon vertex count (3 for each triangle "
"when `generateTriangles=true`); `intersectedEdges` holds the edge tuples in "
"polygon traversal order so the caller can build polygon connectivity by "
"looking up each edge's deduplicated iso-vertex ID."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:241
msgid ""
"**Clip — two-pass Count/Emit.** Used by `vtkTableBasedClipDataSet`. Output "
"point IDs are written directly (combining the kept-point `pointMap` lookup "
"with the iso-vertex `numberOfKeptPoints + edgeId` offset) so the caller can "
"copy the resulting cell arrays into pre-reserved global offsets without a "
"second remapping pass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:247
msgid ""
"static void CountClip(numPointIds, pointIds, polyhedronFaces, scalars,\n"
"    isoValue, insideOut,\n"
"    &numOutputCells, &numOutputCellConnectivity,\n"
"    &numOutputFaces, &numOutputFacesConnectivity,\n"
"    intersectedEdges);\n"
"\n"
"static void EmitClip(numPointIds, pointIds, polyhedronFaces, scalars,\n"
"    isoValue, insideOut, pointMap, numberOfKeptPoints, edgeLocator,\n"
"    outputCells, outputFaces);\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:259
msgid ""
"The clip Count/Emit functions return edge endpoint pairs and interpolation "
"weights rather than interpolated point data, so the calling filter can "
"perform point data interpolation externally in bulk, matching the pattern "
"used by existing VTK threaded filters."
msgstr ""

