#: ../../../design_documents/PolyhedronAlgorithms.md:455
msgid ""
"The plot above is log-log; the dashed line is slope-1 (linear) for "
"reference. Contour wall-time scales sublinearly with input cells: 125x input "
"growth from 100³ to 500³ produces only ~42x growth in contour time. The "
"reason is dimensional: contour input is volumetric (`O(D³)`) but contour "
"output is the iso-surface, which is `O(D²)`. The output-bounded portion of "
"the algorithm therefore grows more slowly than total input work. Clip output "
"is also volumetric (a fraction of the input mesh), so its cost scales close "
"to linearly with input."
msgstr ""

